Title: AROS platform: build, stack, timer, system name, modules without a backend yet
Repository: love
Base: def245102c67909f9902095af613b1ae05249b62
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-19
Author: aros-loeve project
Problem: LÖVE's build knows Windows, macOS, Linux, Android and iOS. On AROS it stopped at "Could not detect target platform", built position-independent code (which AROS cannot load), linked liblove as a shared library, required OpenAL and libmodplug, and had no timer or program path. At run time the Shell's 40 KiB stack overflowed in the shader compiler and SDL's missing sensor support stopped start-up.
Change: LOVE_AROS in config.h; CMake: no PIC, liblove static, no Vulkan backend. Timer from SDL's performance counter, the program path from GetProgramDir, love.system.getOS() is "AROS". src/aros_stack.c runs the program on an 8 MiB stack. love.sensor loads without SDL sensor support and reports no sensors. Not built yet on AROS: OpenAL output (love.audio uses the null backend), libmodplug, enet, luasocket, lua-https.
Scope: AROS (built and run for mainline x86_64); no effect elsewhere
Upstream: candidate once audio and the network libraries work
Verification: Built for mainline AROS x86_64 (GCC 10.5, SDK nightly 20261110) with no implicit function declarations; LÖVE 12.0 ran a test game on pool v1-3 (exec 51.17, softpipe) on 2026-11-19: window, canvas, shader, shapes and a clean exit, seven screen pixels exact
Removal: The "not built yet" parts go as audio and network support arrive.
